# Citation metadata for the public sigmaSPH repository.  GitHub reads it for its "Cite this
# repository" button, and Zenodo reads it for the record of each release.  release.py
# rewrites the version and date-released lines with the release being made; the values here
# are placeholders.  The DOI is Zenodo's concept DOI, which resolves to the latest version.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "sigmaSPH: a GPU-accelerated SPH solver for fluids and elastic-plastic solids"
abstract: >-
  sigmaSPH is a GPU-accelerated Smoothed Particle Hydrodynamics code written in Taichi.
  It simulates weakly compressible fluids with delta-plus-SPH and hypoelastic-plastic
  solids at large deformation, in 3D, 2D plane strain and 2D axisymmetry, with
  Mie-Grueneisen, JWL and Holmquist-Johnson-Cook equations of state, J2 and Johnson-Cook
  plasticity, and Johnson-Cook, Cocks-Ashby, Holmquist-Johnson-Cook and Grady-Kipp damage.
authors:
  - family-names: "Ganzenmüller"
    given-names: "Georg C."
    email: georg.ganzenmueller@inatech.uni-freiburg.de
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5741-8844"
    affiliation: >-
      Institute of Sustainable Systems Engineering (INATECH), University of Freiburg,
      Freiburg, Germany; Fraunhofer Institute for High-Speed Dynamics,
      Ernst-Mach-Institut, EMI, Freiburg, Germany
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23084820
repository-code: "https://github.com/ggalu/sigmaSPH"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - smoothed particle hydrodynamics
  - SPH
  - GPU
  - Taichi
  - solid mechanics
  - hypervelocity impact
  - fracture
version: "v0.1.3"
date-released: "2026-10-01"
